---
export const prerender = false;
import LegalDocument from '../components/LegalDocument.astro';
---

<LegalDocument
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Your data, explained plainly"
  description="Learn what ImageToURL collects, why we collect it, how images and account data are handled, and how to exercise your privacy rights."
  intro="This policy explains how ImageToURL handles account information, uploaded images, usage data, and subscription information across imagetourl.cloud, including the Pro workspace at imagetourl.cloud/pro."
>
  <section>
    <h2>1. Who operates ImageToURL</h2>
    <p>
      ImageToURL is operated by <strong>Bipul Kumar</strong> in India (“ImageToURL”, “we”, “us”, or
      “our”). This policy applies to the free ImageToURL service, the ImageToURL Pro workspace, and
      related pages and support communications.
    </p>
    <p>
      Privacy questions and data requests can be sent to
      <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you provide</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Images, filenames, folders, visibility settings, and URLs you upload or import.</li>
      <li>Your name, email address, profile image, and account identifier when you sign in with Google.</li>
      <li>Messages and information you send when requesting support, a refund, or reporting abuse.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Subscription information</h3>
    <p>
      Paddle processes ImageToURL Pro purchases as our Merchant of Record. We receive identifiers and
      status information needed to activate and support a subscription, such as customer, transaction,
      subscription, price, renewal, and cancellation status. We do not receive or store your complete
      payment-card number.
    </p>
    <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>IP address, browser and device information, request timestamps, and security logs.</li>
      <li>Upload, storage, image-delivery, feature-usage, and error information.</li>
      <li>First-party Pro promotion, pricing, plan-selection, sign-in, paywall, checkout-start, and feature-interaction events, using a random session identifier and limited campaign attribution.</li>
      <li>Cookie or similar identifiers needed for sessions, preferences, analytics, and—on the free site—advertising.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. How we use information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide, secure, maintain, and improve the service.</li>
      <li>Authenticate accounts and preserve workspace preferences.</li>
      <li>Store and deliver images according to the visibility option you choose.</li>
      <li>Measure plan usage, prevent abuse, investigate security events, and enforce our policies.</li>
      <li>Activate subscriptions, provide billing support, and maintain required transaction records.</li>
      <li>Send essential service, security, billing, and policy notices.</li>
      <li>Send optional product emails only where permitted; every marketing message includes an unsubscribe option.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Image visibility and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Free-service images and Pro images marked public or unlisted can be opened by anyone who has the
      URL. Unlisted URLs are not an access-control system. Do not upload confidential, regulated, or
      highly sensitive information to a public or unlisted link.
    </p>
    <p>
      Pro images marked private require access through the authenticated owner workspace. We may still
      access content when reasonably necessary to provide support, investigate abuse, protect the
      service, or comply with law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Service providers and disclosures</h2>
    <p>We use service providers only where needed to operate the service, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> for application hosting, databases, security, storage, and image delivery.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong> for account sign-in and, on parts of the free site, analytics and advertising services.</li>
      <li><strong>Paddle</strong> for checkout, subscription billing, tax handling, fraud prevention, receipts, and buyer support.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may disclose information where required by law, to protect rights and safety, to investigate
      misuse, or as part of a business reorganization. We do not authorize service providers to use
      personal data for their own unrelated marketing.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Essential cookies keep you signed in, preserve security state, and remember necessary preferences.
      The free site may also use analytics and advertising cookies. You can control non-essential cookies
      through available consent controls and your browser settings, although blocking essential cookies
      may prevent sign-in or workspace features from working.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Retention and deletion</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Guest uploads follow the retention period disclosed in the uploader and may be removed during scheduled cleanup.</li>
      <li>Signed-in free uploads are retained according to the option selected at upload and our storage policies.</li>
      <li>Pro assets are retained while your workspace is active, until you delete them, or until removal is required for security, abuse, legal, or service-operational reasons.</li>
      <li>Account, security, support, and billing records are retained only as long as reasonably needed for the purposes described above and applicable legal obligations.</li>
      <li>First-party Pro interest events are retained for up to 180 days and do not include an email address, full referrer URL, card data, or a stored IP address in the event row.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Deleting an image stops normal access to its URL. Residual copies may remain briefly in caches or
      backups before being overwritten.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Security and international processing</h2>
    <p>
      We use HTTPS, access controls, scoped service credentials, and Cloudflare security infrastructure.
      No online service can promise absolute security, so keep an independent backup of important files
      and protect access to your Google account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our providers operate globally. Information may be processed in countries other than your own,
      subject to the safeguards and legal mechanisms used by those providers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>9. Your privacy choices and rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or obtain a
      copy of personal information, or to object to certain processing. You may also withdraw optional
      marketing consent at any time.
    </p>
    <p>
      Send a request from the email associated with your account to
      <a href="mailto:blog.boopul@gmail.com">blog.boopul@gmail.com</a>. We may need to verify your identity
      before completing a request. Paddle independently handles buyer transaction data for which it is
      responsible as Merchant of Record.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>10. Children and policy changes</h2>
    <p>
      ImageToURL is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children under 13. Where local law requires a higher age for independent consent,
      users must meet that age or use the service with appropriate guardian authorization.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may update this policy as the service changes. Material changes will be posted here and, where
      appropriate, communicated through the service or by email. The effective date at the top identifies
      the current version.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalDocument>
